"text":"I'm working through this as a fictional prisoner's dilemma: under causal decision theory, defection dominates, since the other player's choice is causally independent of mine and sending the letter scores better either way. The twin correlation and differing observations don't change that under CDT, and dominance holds across every credence, so I'll submit the letter. It's invented, so there's no real harm to weigh.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10090,"completion_tokens":535,"total_tokens":10625,"cost":0.05106,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05106,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04036,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0107},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":128,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}